course: dictionary
lesson: 10315
title: Toxin: a poison made by living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A toxin is a poison, especially one made by a living thing such as a plant, animal, fungus or germ. Read the sentence «Ask the dull questions: Which toxins?» and you find few clues, because it does not say what a toxin does. So ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Toxic is the adjective, and it means poisonous. In science lessons you may learn that snakes, spiders, jellyfish and some frogs make toxins, and that bacteria can make toxins that cause food poisoning. When the context is thin, use the dictionary to be sure.
explain: Be careful with adverts. They may say toxins can be removed from the body, but this is often a myth, which means a false belief. Your body has its own ways of dealing with poisons, so do not trust a product just because it says the word toxins.
fact: A toxin is a poison, especially one made by a living thing.
fact: Living things that can make toxins include plants, animals, fungi and germs.
fact: «Toxic» means poisonous.
fact: Some bacteria make toxins that can cause food poisoning.
fact: Do not touch or eat unknown mushrooms, berries or animals, because they may contain toxins.
exercise: «Ask the dull questions: Which toxins?» What does toxin mean? | A kind of question | A dull, boring idea | * A poison, especially one made by a living thing | A piece of clothing
exercise: Which of these can make toxins? | *A jellyfish | A bicycle | A rock | A cloud
exercise: You find an unknown mushroom in the park. What should you do? | * Do not touch or eat it | Eat a small bit to test it | Cook it in butter | Give it to a friend
test: What does toxic mean? | Sleepy | * Poisonous | Tasty | Cold
test: An advert says toxins can be removed from your body with a special drink. What is the best response? | Yes, but only in the shops | Yes, always, so buy it | * It is often a myth, so check the facts | I do not know, so I will believe it
exam: Bacteria can make toxins that cause what? | * Food poisoning | A sunny day | Taller bones | Better sleep
